+# Crash- and network-safe local meeting capture
+
+**Feature:** `meeting-capture-durability`
+**Issue:** `d88d461a-c259-4dc6-a751-f2b3c6898b7a`
+**Date:** 2026-08-10
+**Classification:** Critical — recorded audio, tenant authorization, browser persistence, retention, and finalization correctness
+**Status:** PLAN revised after independent review; human approval and mandatory dependency gates are required before DEV
+**Base:** `origin/main@5a4ed8d8f52b7fe78044fac000602b9cd6552ee0`
+**Branch/worktree:** `codex/meeting-capture-durability-plan` / `.worktrees/meeting-capture-durability-plan`
+
+## Outcome
+
+Make the existing botless browser microphone capture resilient to renderer crashes, reloads, and transient network loss. Each slice is committed to an origin-scoped IndexedDB outbox before it becomes upload-eligible, identified by an immutable `capture_session_id` plus a zero-based monotonic `sequence`, retried idempotently, and deleted locally only after a matching durable server acknowledgement.
+
+This issue owns durable capture completion: after the server proves the full terminal sequence is contiguous, it returns a versioned `meeting.capture.completed` result/event. Issue `ce942338-35af-4960-ae83-ebc55bdbbe2a` consumes that event later and exclusively owns meeting status compatibility, final summary/chapters/candidates, rendered-artifact refresh, and transcript-to-action proof. It is not an input dependency of this plan.
+
+This issue does not add a bot, provider SDK, local AI, native desktop audio, a new transcription engine, or a second meeting authority.
+
+## Verified baseline
+
+- `apps/meeting-web/src/hooks/useAudioRecorder.js` emits WAV blobs on a timer and resets in-memory `chunkIndexRef` to zero on every recording start.
+- `apps/meeting-web/src/App.jsx` sends each blob immediately through `transcribeAudio`; a failed request is toasted but not persisted or retried across reload.
+- `packages/sdk/src/meeting.js` maps that call to `POST /meetings/{meeting_id}/transcribe` with `chunk_index`, `elapsed_seconds`, and `chunk_duration_seconds`.
+- `apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py` authenticates and owner-scopes the meeting, optionally archives audio, transcribes inline, inserts fresh transcript segment IDs, and returns `chunk_index`. It has no `capture_session_id`, digest-bound idempotency, durable raw-slice ACK, gap status, or capture-complete event.
+- Canonical `audio_assets` lacks capture-session/sequence/digest/contiguous-ledger fields. Neither it nor `jobs.payload` is an acceptable substitute for the canonical capture ledger.
+
+## Mandatory external entry gate: `ce3127d7...`
+
+No server or browser implementation slice in this plan may start until issue `ce3127d7-2ae0-4eff-aa37-1101762d0d0b` is:
+
+1. separately planned and human-approved through the Neon/Drizzle authority lane;
+2. implemented, migrated, rollback-tested, security-tested, and merged;
+3. present on current `origin/main` at an exact recorded landed SHA;
+4. publishing an immutable raw-slice read handle/stream plus a durable post-commit STT work-claim contract with restart/startup recovery. The dependency must prove crash-after-ACK-before-scheduling recovery, missing or expired raw objects, duplicate worker delivery, and retention-versus-processing races without weakening raw ACK semantics.
+5. verified to provide tenant-bound capture sessions, unique `(capture_session_id, sequence)`, digest conflict protection, durable raw-slice acceptance, contiguous watermark/gaps, immutable terminal intent, consent/provenance/retention/deletion fields, and concurrency/idempotency semantics; and
+6. accompanied by the exact canonical repository/adapter file paths that downstream server tasks may own.
+
+There is no `jobs.payload` fallback, in-memory fallback, filename/metadata encoding, parallel table, raw SQL side path, or provisional browser-only endpoint. If the landed schema/adapter contract differs from this plan, return to PLAN before DEV. Server task ownership remains deliberately deferred to the exact adapter files published by the landed dependency; this document does not invent them.
+
+## Selected server acknowledgement and processing semantics
+
+The product roadmap calls for slice-and-queue capture where persistence, not transcription latency, defines delivery correctness.
+
+### Raw acceptance ledger
+
+- The canonical ledger exposes `reserved -> processing -> acknowledged | failed` recovery states from `ce3127d7...`.
+- `acknowledged` means both the raw slice and its canonical ledger mutation committed durably. The API must never return a valid slice ACK before that commit.
+- If raw object storage and the ledger cannot commit atomically, the landed dependency must define a recoverable reservation/reconciliation protocol. A precommit `2xx`, optimistic ACK, transcript response, object existence guess, or queued job is never an ACK.
+- Identical `(capture_session_id, sequence, digest)` replay returns the same raw-acceptance result. Same session/sequence with changed digest or immutable metadata is a terminal conflict.
+- Out-of-order raw slices may reach `acknowledged`, but `contiguous_through` advances only across a gap-free prefix.
+
+### Asynchronous idempotent STT
+
+- Transcription begins only from committed `acknowledged` raw slices and is asynchronous relative to the client ACK.
+- STT claim/retry is idempotent by the canonical slice identity and cannot create duplicate transcript evidence.
+- Retryable STT failure does not revoke a valid raw ACK or make the browser retain an already-ACKed Blob. It remains observable/retryable server work.
+- A raw acceptance `failed` state never produces an ACK. The status contract distinguishes raw acceptance failure from downstream STT state without returning transcript/audio content.
+
+### Capture finalize
+
+- Stop first persists the final partial slice and immutable `expected_terminal_sequence`.
+- Finalize succeeds only when server status proves `0..expected_terminal_sequence` raw-ACKed contiguously.
+- Repeated identical finalize converges. A different terminal sequence conflicts.
+- Success emits/returns versioned `meeting.capture.completed/v1` containing only the server-derived meeting/capture identity, immutable terminal sequence, contiguous boundary, contract version, and server completion time or the exact landed equivalent.
+- This result ends d88's authority. `ce942338...` later consumes it for summary/candidate/artifact finalization; d88 neither waits for nor implements those outcomes.
+
+## Success criteria
+
+1. `ce3127d7...` is landed on `origin/main` at an exact recorded SHA before any d88 server/browser DEV work; implementation uses only its published canonical adapters and never `jobs.payload`.
+2. A captured slice becomes upload-eligible only after its IndexedDB write transaction completes. Persistence failure prevents all later sequence emission and retains the uncommitted recorder buffer for retry/stop handling.
+3. Records are keyed by `[capture_session_id, sequence]`; sequence is monotonic, immutable, and never reset for a recovered session. Blob, digest, timing, MIME, consent/provenance references, retry metadata, and state survive reload.
+4. The server returns ACK only after raw slice plus canonical ledger commit. Identical replay converges; changed replay conflicts; async STT cannot delay, manufacture, revoke, or duplicate raw ACK.
+5. Exactly one foreground drain lease uploads a session with bounded concurrency. Offline, timeout, `429`, and retryable `5xx` remain durable and resume on reload, explicit retry, foreground hints, or optional Background Sync.
+6. The client deletes a local Blob only in a transaction that validates ACK session, sequence, digest, and contract version. Lost ACK causes safe replay.
+7. Stop awaits a serialized, awaitable recorder flush. The final buffer is not cleared until its IndexedDB transaction completes; final sequence is frozen only after that durable commit.
+8. Durable capture finalize is idempotent and gap-gated, and returns the versioned capture-complete result/event. Missing middle slices, authorization changes, conflicts, and partial raw acceptance never render capture complete.
+9. Consent remains explicit and visible. Capture cannot begin/resume under a different user/tenant, after logout, or without server-bound consent/provenance. Reload never restarts microphone capture automatically.
+10. Quota/backpressure is bounded and visible. `QuotaExceededError`, denied storage, unsupported APIs, delayed IndexedDB, or high backlog pauses capture before silent loss.
+11. Server capability and browser rollout flag are explicit and tested. Flag-off blocks only new Start/session creation; existing outboxes can drain, reconcile, finalize, and delete throughout the declared recovery window.
+12. ACKed local audio is removed promptly; unACKed recovery data has bounded expiry and explicit discard. Logs/telemetry contain state/counters/timings/error classes only and never sensitive content or raw identifiers.
+13. Deterministic tests cover delayed/rejected IndexedDB, stop during flush, offline/reload, duplicates, out-of-order delivery, lost ACK, STT retry, quota/backpressure, auth/tenant change, discard/retention, missing sequence, capture-complete replay, and flag rollback; affected fast and full gates pass at their stage.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- RealtimeKit rooms, Recall, Zoom RTMS, LiveKit talkback/agents, participant bots, calendar recognition, Chrome extension capture, and provider-owned durable state.
+- Tauri/native desktop audio, native encrypted spools, OS credential stores, WASAPI, Core Audio, PipeWire, signing, installers, and updaters.
+- Local transcription, summarization, diarization, candidates, work-item creation, or any local AI.
+- Unified chat, caller-authority review UI, `Add`/`Adjust`/`Dismiss`, and promotion.
+- Schema/migration/repository design owned by `ce3127d7...`; d88 only consumes its exact landed adapters.
+- Meeting summary/chapter/candidate/artifact finalization owned by `ce942338...`.
+- Service Worker or Background Sync as a correctness dependency.
+
+## Three approaches
+
+### A. Memory queue with retry timers
+
+Smallest diff, but reload/crash loses blobs, duplicate ownership across tabs is undefined, and it cannot meet persist-before-send.
+
+### B. IndexedDB transactional outbox with foreground drain — selected
+
+Persist each immutable slice envelope before send; recover/drain on boot and foreground; use the canonical ledger for idempotent raw ACK, status reconciliation, and capture finalize. This is the smallest design that makes crash recovery and upload retry the same state machine.
+
+### C. Service Worker owns all delivery
+
+Potentially improves closed-tab upload but adds worker lifecycle/versioning complexity and depends on Background Sync that is not broadly available. The selected outbox can later be drained by a worker without changing correctness.
+
+## Browser design
+
+### Data flow
+
+```text
+explicit Start + auth + server-bound consent + capability/flag gate
+                              |
+                      recorder WAV buffer
+                              |
+                 serialized awaitable flush queue
+                              |
+              IndexedDB readwrite durable commit
+              (slice + next_sequence atomically)
+                              |
+                    upload-eligible outbox row
+                              |
+             authenticated canonical raw ingest
+                              |
+            raw slice + canonical ledger commit
+                              |
+ matching ACK + contiguous boundary + contract version
+                              |
+          validate ACK then delete local Blob atomically
+                              |
+ Stop -> await final flush -> freeze terminal sequence
+                              |
+ status reconcile -> gap-free -> capture finalize
+                              |
+             meeting.capture.completed/v1
+                              |
+     later ce942 consumes for summaries/candidates/artifacts
+```
+
+### IndexedDB model and invariants
+
+Use the native IndexedDB API behind a small repository. Exact object-store names/version are implementation details fixed by tests.
+
+- **sessions**, keyed by `capture_session_id`: meeting reference, server contract/capability version, consent/provenance reference, `next_sequence`, expected terminal sequence, contiguous boundary, state, drain lease, expiry, and non-secret auth-subject binding reference.
+- **slices**, keyed by `[capture_session_id, sequence]`: Blob, digest, MIME/codec, timing, bytes, state, attempts, retry time, and redacted error class.
+
+One readwrite transaction stores the slice and advances `next_sequence`. Only transaction completion resolves the flush promise and authorizes upload. The standard `durability: "strict"` hint is used when supported, with feature detection.
+
+The recorder flush path is a single serialized promise chain:
+
+1. snapshot current audio samples without discarding them;
+2. await digest/envelope creation;
+3. await IndexedDB commit;
+4. only then clear exactly those samples and allow the next sequence;
+5. on rejection, retain the samples, block later emission, pause capture, and surface recovery/error; and
+6. Stop awaits the active flush, then enqueues/awaits the final partial flush before freezing `expected_terminal_sequence`.
+
+Tests use controlled deferred/rejected transactions to prove sequence `N+1` cannot appear while `N` is unresolved, a rejected flush does not discard its buffer, concurrent timer/Stop flushes serialize, and Stop cannot finalize before the final durable commit.
+
+A leased foreground drainer prevents ordinary multi-tab duplication; server idempotency remains mandatory because leases expire during crashes. Reload validates all records as untrusted, reauthenticates, reconciles status, and asks the user to resume drain/discard. It never calls `getUserMedia` automatically.
+
+### Quota and backpressure
+
+- Use `navigator.storage.estimate()` before Start and periodically; reserve headroom because values are approximate.
+- Request `navigator.storage.persist()` only through explicit capture/recovery UX and report denial honestly.
+- Production byte/backlog limits come from the landed capability/codec contract; tests inject small deterministic caps.
+- Default to one in-flight slice per session unless the server capability declares otherwise. Honor `Retry-After` and bounded jittered backoff.
+- At high-water or write failure, pause before accepting more samples. Never discard a buffer or continue recording without durable capacity.
+- `online`, focus, visibility, and optional Background Sync are wake hints only. Never begin IndexedDB work from unload handlers.
+
+### Capability and rollout flag
+
+The server owns capability `meeting_capture_durability_v1` in the existing runtime-config/capability surface (`packages/contracts/src/meeting.js`, `apps/meeting-api/backend/routes/runtime.py`, registration in `apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py`). It declares contract version, new-session availability, recovery operations, and limits. The browser owns normalized flag `durableCaptureEnabled` in `apps/meeting-web/src/lib/runtimeConfig.js` and consumes both flag and server capability.
+
+Start/create requires **both** browser flag on and a compatible server capability. Recovery operations are separate and remain enabled for sessions already present locally/server-side even when new-session availability or the browser flag is off. Tests prove flag-off/capability-off rejects only new Start/create while old outboxes still call ingest/status/finalize/delete during the recovery window. Removing recovery capability before the window closes is a release blocker, not rollback.
+
+### Consent, authority, provenance, retention
+
+- Start is an explicit user action with the existing visible recording indicator.
+- Session creation binds server-derived actor/tenant, meeting, immutable consent evidence, source/provenance, codec, and retention before the recorder starts.
+- IndexedDB stores no token, credential, or client-selected tenant/owner. Current auth is checked for every drain/finalize/delete.
+- Logout or subject change releases the local lease and blocks upload; another user cannot adopt the session.
+- ACKed Blobs delete promptly. UnACKed Blobs follow the landed recovery retention and remain visible for discard. Offline local discard must not claim remote deletion.
+- Browser storage is not confidential against same-origin XSS, local profile access, malware, or user-cleared site data. Privacy relies on minimization, short retention, CSP/XSS controls, and accurate disclosure.
+
+### Observability and redaction
+
+Allowed: random diagnostic correlation, app/build/contract version, state transition, sequence count/range, queued bytes/count/age, raw-acceptance/STT state, retry/error class, status class, ACK/contiguous latency, flush/drain/finalize duration, quota/persistence and flag/capability outcome.
+
+Forbidden: audio/Blob, transcript/summary/candidate text, tokens/cookies/headers, raw meeting/session/user/tenant IDs, participant/calendar/consent content, digest, filename, storage path, signed URL, provider response, or exception body containing them.
+
+## Security/privacy pass
+
+| Risk | Required mitigation |
+|---|---|
+| OWASP A01 access control | Server derives actor/tenant and checks meeting/session on create/ingest/status/finalize/delete; foreign resources remain undisclosed. |
+| A02 local confidentiality | HTTPS; no token in IndexedDB; minimum retention; do not claim browser encryption as a boundary. |
+| A03 injection/untrusted storage | Validate IndexedDB and multipart data identically; fixed codec/size contract; no client filesystem/path authority. |
+| A04 insecure design | Canonical ledger prerequisite, no precommit ACK, serialized persist-before-send, digest conflict, ACK-validated deletion, gap-gated capture finalize. |
+| A05 misconfiguration | Secure context, explicit capability/flag, bounded limits, no wildcard CORS/debug audio, recovery preserved during rollback. |
+| A06 components | Native IndexedDB; no storage dependency without separate review. |
+| A07 auth | Authenticate every operation; block logout/subject change; never store bearer tokens with audio. |
+| A08 integrity | Immutable identity/digest/terminal sequence; idempotent raw/STT/finalize; validate reloaded state. |
+| A09 monitoring | Redacted state metrics and conflict/security events; test log canaries and telemetry failures. |
+| A10 SSRF | Configured meeting API only; storage paths/URLs never client-selectable. |
+
+## Seven-PR ordered train
+
+Every PR is independently reversible and targets <=300 changed production-code lines excluding tests, docs, generated files, and lockfiles. Each begins only after its predecessor lands on `origin/main` and its exact SHA is recorded.
+
