+Server canonical adapter ownership is intentionally not guessed. Before PR2/3/4 DEV, copy the exact `ce3127d7...` landed paths into the Forge issue and each PR's ownership list. If that creates >300 production lines or overlaps another active owner, split within the same ordered train only after PLAN amendment.
+
+## Validation matrix
+
+| Case | Expected proof |
+|---|---|
+| Delayed IndexedDB | No upload or sequence `N+1`; buffer remains until `N` transaction completes. |
+| Rejected IndexedDB | Buffer not discarded; later sequence blocked; recorder pauses; Stop reports blocked, never complete. |
+| Timer flush races Stop | One serialized chain; Stop awaits active flush and final partial durable commit. |
+| Offline/reload | Pending row survives; foreground recovery drains after current-auth reconciliation without auto-recording. |
+| Lost response after raw commit | Identical replay returns same ACK; local deletion follows matching response; STT still runs once. |
+| Precommit failure | No ACK, no local deletion, recoverable reserved/processing/failed state per canonical ledger. |
+| Duplicate / changed duplicate | Identical converges; changed digest conflicts and retains local Blob. |
+| Out of order `0,2,1` | Individual raw ACKs allowed; boundary stays `0`, then advances through `2`; finalize blocked until gap closes. |
+| Async STT retry/failure | Raw ACK remains valid; idempotent retry does not duplicate transcript; status distinguishes failure. |
+| Missing final/middle slice | Capture finalize fails precondition and emits no capture-complete event. |
+| Repeated capture finalize | Same terminal request/event converges; changed terminal conflicts. |
+| Two tabs | One local lease; forced race remains safe through server idempotency. |
+| Quota/high backlog | New capture pauses before loss; recovery/discard remains available. |
+| Auth/tenant change | Drain/finalize/delete block; no authority transfer or foreign-resource disclosure. |
+| Flag/capability off after capture | New Start/create blocked; existing outbox still ingests, reconciles, finalizes, and deletes. |
+| Recovery window expiry | New starts already off; operator sees remaining recoveries; capability removal remains blocked until policy satisfied. |
+| Privacy canaries | Logs/telemetry contain no forbidden values, even on malformed local/server errors. |
+
+## Rollout and rollback
+
+1. Land/verify `ce3127d7...`; no d88 code before its exact SHA is recorded.
+2. Land PR1 capability/flag off by default.
+3. Land server PRs with synthetic audio in non-production and recovery APIs enabled.
+4. Land browser persistence/flush/drain PRs; internal allowlist only.
+5. Measure raw ACK latency, reservation recovery, contiguous lag, STT retry, backlog/quota, flag state, and recovery-window population before widening.
+
+Rollback always sets new-session availability and the browser flag off first. It never disables compatible ingest/status/finalize/delete for existing sessions until the declared recovery window closes and remaining recoveries are resolved. It never clears IndexedDB, drops ledger state, restores direct fire-and-forget `/transcribe` for durable sessions, or treats downstream transcript/summary success as raw ACK.
+
+## Dependencies and sequencing
+
+- Mandatory prerequisite: `ce3127d7-2ae0-4eff-aa37-1101762d0d0b`, exact landed SHA before PR1 and before all server/browser slices.
+- d88 owns raw durability, async STT triggering/idempotency, gap status, capture finalize, and versioned capture-complete result/event.
+- `ce942338...` depends on and consumes d88 later. It owns meeting terminal status compatibility, final summary/chapters/candidates, artifacts, and transcript-to-action E2E. d88 does not depend on it.
+- External connector and desktop lanes consume the landed d88 contract later.
+
+## Human DEV checkpoint
+
+Approval must explicitly confirm:
+
+1. `ce3127d7...` is human-approved, merged, and present on current `origin/main` at an exact SHA, with canonical adapter paths and no `jobs.payload` fallback.
+2. ACK means raw slice plus canonical ledger commit; `reserved/processing/acknowledged/failed` recovery and async idempotent STT semantics are accepted.
+3. d88 owns versioned capture-complete; `ce942338...` is a downstream consumer, not an entry gate.
+4. Serialized recorder flush semantics, quota/backpressure behavior, and delayed/rejected-IDB test matrix are accepted.
+5. Seven ordered <=300-production-line PRs, exact known ownership, deferred canonical adapter ownership, and per-PR rollback are accepted.
+6. `meeting_capture_durability_v1` plus `durableCaptureEnabled` rollout behavior preserves old-session recovery when new Start/create is off.
+7. Privacy/retention/redaction and the recovery-window policy are approved.
+
+No gate is approved by this PLAN. DEV must re-prove the lease, rebase on current `origin/main`, record the dependency SHA and exact paths, and start PR1 only after human approval.
+
+## Ambiguity policy
+
+Use the `/dev` seven-dimension rubric. Below 80% confidence, or for any change to dependency/schema/adapter paths, endpoint/event fields, ACK boundary, STT state, codec, retention, consent, auth, tenant derivation, flag/recovery, finalize, or deletion semantics, stop and return to human PLAN review.
+
+## Technical sources
+
+- [Indexed Database API 3.0](https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/) — transactional atomicity, durability hints, ordered requests, and commit/abort behavior.
+- [MDN: Using IndexedDB](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/IndexedDB_API/Using_IndexedDB) — same-origin storage and why asynchronous unload transactions are unsafe.
+- [MDN: Storage quotas and eviction criteria](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Storage_API/Storage_quotas_and_eviction_criteria) and [StorageManager.estimate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/StorageManager/estimate) — best-effort/persistent storage, approximate quotas, eviction, and `QuotaExceededError`.
+- [MDN: Background Synchronization API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Background_Synchronization_API) — limited availability; optional enhancement only.
+- [OWASP HTML5 Security Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTML5_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html) — IndexedDB is accessible to same-origin XSS/local profile access and must be treated as untrusted.
+- [OWASP File Upload Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/File_Upload_Cheat_Sheet.html) and [Logging Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Logging_Cheat_Sheet.html) — authorize/validate uploads and exclude sensitive data from logs.
